  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1) \nRiver valley fog will burn off shortly after daybreak this morning.\nWe may continue to observe some cirrus clouds in our CWA as they\npivot around the upper low off the Atlantic Coast. The Ohio Valley\nremains in the dry slot of this low, which continues to sit and spin\nbefore it gets carried off to the northeast early in the work week. \n\nReturn flow develops after the low is carried off, which will result\nin a warming trend as we progress through the work week. Temperatures\nwill likely be back above seasonal normals by Wednesday. \n\nRain chances look to return on Thursday as a boundary lays out \nacross the Midwest region. Rain chances look to persist through next \nweekend.",
